<!-- Couperin, Concerts royaux III Courante m5 (1722 review N-R15): slurs from an upper-voice quarter to the next
     eighth of the lower voice, whose down stems are beamed under the noteheads. The 1722 print draws each as a short
     arc from notehead to notehead, over the beam. The third slur (A5 to D5, over three notes) is a regular slur. -->
